{title: Behold, How Good}
{subtitle: Psalm 133}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 120}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [A] |
| [A] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Behold how good, behold how good
When brothers [Gm]dwell in unity
[Dm]Behold how good, behold how good
How good and how [C]pleasant [A]it is
And how pleasant when we [C]dwell as one
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Be[Bb]hold how [C]good, behold how good, how good and pleas[C]ant it is
[Bb]Behold [C]how good, behold how good, when we dwell as one
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Like the oil upon the head of Aaron
Like the dew upon Mount Zion
There the Lord com[Gm]mands the [C]blessing
Life fore[Dm]vermore
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Behold [C]how good, behold [Bb]how good
[C]How good and pleasant it is
Behold [C]how good, be[Bb]hold how [C]good
When we dwell as [Dm]one
{end_of_chorus}

